[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-123269"] :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y),$ traversed along the line segment from $(1,3)$ to $(0,3)?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{t}_{a}}^{{t}_{b}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is the line segment from $(1,3)$ to $(0,3).$ \n\nThe position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=i+3\\,j$ and $b=3\\,j.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =(i+3\\,j)+t[3\\,j-(i+3\\,j)] \\\\  & =(i+3\\,j)-t\\,i \\\\  & =(1-t)\\,i+3\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x=1-t$ and $y=3$ along the segment.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3)j \\\\  & =-i \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡((1-t)+3) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4-t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4-t)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(4-t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-123283/selection/69c89053735d600f928caac1a0da43cce7f642e40c4696729c933d8612b50866" :answer/id #uuid "4bc7c57c-34ae-5f0c-a5a3-e35485f62127" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123283/selection/8d22265acda8af43b138941143b7d02314856f82301293d96c1b62829252b947" :answer/id #uuid "305ee261-686a-58b8-ab44-0a1628191306" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123283/selection/5ad4f51cd2387f7927a6a9f3932e21f27fc69df2fcc9ae7470c437c854560b7c" :answer/id #uuid "054c274f-e084-5711-8e0d-43c62b9f0a14" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{7t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123283/selection/fc03d6e35ced1892cac7e386014e2c5a0c18a047529a177e7a18726a8c8bfd02" :answer/id #uuid "9740a1bd-cf0f-55ee-b11b-7959b228e28a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{7t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123283/selection/84ea168055a4b91b45f72761cdaa208f0b629db473df98e4b8b9e7c666e61888" :answer/id #uuid "881f55e9-5b7b-55e9-92d6-a6d527b78b2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123283/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8e6de5a2-2123-5037-884d-69c621275f0d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123283/selection/8d22265acda8af43b138941143b7d02314856f82301293d96c1b62829252b947" :answer-field/choices ["q-123283/selection/69c89053735d600f928caac1a0da43cce7f642e40c4696729c933d8612b50866" "q-123283/selection/8d22265acda8af43b138941143b7d02314856f82301293d96c1b62829252b947" "q-123283/selection/5ad4f51cd2387f7927a6a9f3932e21f27fc69df2fcc9ae7470c437c854560b7c" "q-123283/selection/fc03d6e35ced1892cac7e386014e2c5a0c18a047529a177e7a18726a8c8bfd02" "q-123283/selection/84ea168055a4b91b45f72761cdaa208f0b629db473df98e4b8b9e7c666e61888"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123283" :question/id #uuid "b2a142a9-d042-56b2-ba86-b30a7fb0dfd2" :question/math-academy-id "q-123283" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the line integral of the function $f(x,y)={e}^{x+y},$ traversed along the line segment from $(0,0)$ to $(-3,4)?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{t}_{a}}^{{t}_{b}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is the line segment from $(0,0)$ to $(-3,4).$ \n\nThe position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=0$ and $b=-3\\,i+4\\,j.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =0+t\\,(b-0) \\\\  & =t(b) \\\\  & =t(-3\\,i+4\\,j) \\\\  & =-3t\\,i+4t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x=-3t$ and $y=4t$ along the segment.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-3t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t)j \\\\  & =-3\\,i+4\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={e}^{x+y}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & ={e}^{-3t+4t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{t}\\cdot 5\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =5{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-123283/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "189f51d6-494f-515a-bf77-59496421b093"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123283"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123268/selection/a9bf20b17d01eb65492d9d7c0ed86e2c0b8138bec6d440eccb2b36d6cfea054d" :answer/id #uuid "fd5c8f1e-9cdd-5c2b-be42-7f710e33cbac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(t-1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123268/selection/fdf16e957307335c596fa7dc4407cfb15df7d0f7ce0ed9b9b8d89b96e7af23d4" :answer/id #uuid "44cedf87-1924-577e-bcb7-f19e38e1f837" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1))\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123268/selection/ea0fc35c236a6f3eb751708de193e8080c89c9ff7596161cc11f9e4bfeb4f508" :answer/id #uuid "7604eb67-3a25-5d64-9d28-353e85f639b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1))\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123268/selection/3505c375301042bf8d3c9bff9a2a631e44c687dfc9bb61fbb5a96f237ea25d78" :answer/id #uuid "f26d57a2-f43c-530e-92e2-944309574a5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5{\\int }_{0}^{1}(t-1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123268/selection/9d10a6e6863d57cf1f46f88719e8e6d36b867f8b157ce57a8530731a86fd4d51" :answer/id #uuid "a4f1b4b7-f30d-5d18-85dd-96ea2ac0257c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123268/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c8fdd9b5-3078-52cf-b6c4-705bdff70966" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123268/selection/ea0fc35c236a6f3eb751708de193e8080c89c9ff7596161cc11f9e4bfeb4f508" :answer-field/choices ["q-123268/selection/a9bf20b17d01eb65492d9d7c0ed86e2c0b8138bec6d440eccb2b36d6cfea054d" "q-123268/selection/fdf16e957307335c596fa7dc4407cfb15df7d0f7ce0ed9b9b8d89b96e7af23d4" "q-123268/selection/ea0fc35c236a6f3eb751708de193e8080c89c9ff7596161cc11f9e4bfeb4f508" "q-123268/selection/3505c375301042bf8d3c9bff9a2a631e44c687dfc9bb61fbb5a96f237ea25d78" "q-123268/selection/9d10a6e6863d57cf1f46f88719e8e6d36b867f8b157ce57a8530731a86fd4d51"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123268" :question/id #uuid "73f8190a-1ee8-5d13-aa8b-d7ce5ce6bf90" :question/math-academy-id "q-123268" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=1+x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,$ traversed along the line segment from $(-1,1)$ to $(1,2)?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{t}_{a}}^{{t}_{b}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is the line segment from $(-1,1)$ to $(1,2).$ \n\nThe position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=-i+j$ and $b=i+2\\,j.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =(-i+j)+t[(i+2\\,j)-(-i+j)] \\\\  & =(-i+j)+t(2\\,i+j) \\\\  & =(2t-1)\\,i+(t+1)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x=2t-1$ and $y=t+1$ along the segment.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-1)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1)j \\\\  & =2\\,i+j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=1+x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =1+(2t-1)-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1) \\\\  & =2t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1))\\cdot \\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1))\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-123268/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "189f51d6-494f-515a-bf77-59496421b093"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123268"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-123127"] :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the line integral of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-y,$ traversed along the line segment from $(0,2)$ to $(3,1)?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{t}_{a}}^{{t}_{b}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is the line segment from $(0,2)$ to $(3,1).$ \n\nThe position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=2\\,j$ and $b=3\\,i+j.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =2\\,j+t[(3\\,i+j)-2\\,j] \\\\  & =2\\,j+t(3\\,i-j) \\\\  & =3t\\,i+(2-t)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x=3t$ and $y=2-t$ along the segment.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2-t)j \\\\  & =3\\,i-j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(3t)^{2}-(2-t) \\\\  & =9{t}^{2}+t-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(9{t}^{2}+t-2)\\cdot \\sqrt{10}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(9{t}^{2}+t-2)\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-123279/selection/76826e7d5e5d75d2dad4f31c506b9bfea52ffa03d13bb53d01b24181793a237e" :answer/id #uuid "538335b3-3517-5f5a-b3f7-b33eeefc6dd8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{29}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(12t-5)\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123279/selection/16090102b642573e59bf0b52fc48350f26148a887bca31783cead9465d05a210" :answer/id #uuid "a4b507eb-9043-58e2-b3ba-56af466fec8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(8t+7)\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123279/selection/d75e3de086c6bb04310cceafeba54e41b81b0c72b3450f793f9d487e4137aafc" :answer/id #uuid "d5a578bf-d4be-5c93-bd6b-0f6050ef4c90" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{29}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(8t+7)\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123279/selection/e0ac61c5f3b31ae0ce97c6c24e046f16e15597af356a44643fd43d2912287930" :answer/id #uuid "1214e941-a67b-5ed3-8fe9-47147afb9636" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(12t-5)\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123279/selection/430cf79c2175e7262507f9e2845670274b34a804389fbba3d83f476b4f966150" :answer/id #uuid "4e14682b-0fd3-532d-a8b1-d12d14e2a63a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "29{\\int }_{0}^{1}(10t-3)\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123279/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "50490e6c-923c-5571-b6b9-9ce2bf949560" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123279/selection/76826e7d5e5d75d2dad4f31c506b9bfea52ffa03d13bb53d01b24181793a237e" :answer-field/choices ["q-123279/selection/76826e7d5e5d75d2dad4f31c506b9bfea52ffa03d13bb53d01b24181793a237e" "q-123279/selection/16090102b642573e59bf0b52fc48350f26148a887bca31783cead9465d05a210" "q-123279/selection/d75e3de086c6bb04310cceafeba54e41b81b0c72b3450f793f9d487e4137aafc" "q-123279/selection/e0ac61c5f3b31ae0ce97c6c24e046f16e15597af356a44643fd43d2912287930" "q-123279/selection/430cf79c2175e7262507f9e2845670274b34a804389fbba3d83f476b4f966150"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123279" :question/id #uuid "ad9b1481-cda7-5cfd-b724-b43060c478da" :question/math-academy-id "q-123279" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the line integral of the function $f(x,y)=2x+y,$ traversed along the line segment from $(-3,1)$ to $(2,3)?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{t}_{a}}^{{t}_{b}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is the line segment from $(-3,1)$ to $(2,3).$ \n\nThe position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=-3\\,i+j$ and $b=2\\,i+3\\,j.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =(-3\\,i+j)+t[(2\\,i+3\\,j)-(-3\\,i+j)] \\\\  & =(-3\\,i+j)+t(5\\,i+2\\,j) \\\\  & =(5t-3)\\,i+(1+2t)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x=5t-3$ and $y=1+2t$ along the segment.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5t-3)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+2t)j \\\\  & =5\\,i+2\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=2x+y$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2(5t-3)+(1+2t) \\\\  & =12t-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(12t-5)\\cdot \\sqrt{29}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(12t-5)\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-123279/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "189f51d6-494f-515a-bf77-59496421b093"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123279"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76605/selection/6e19974eead0c31037cccb7d9eb05399ff73cc4f9cbc11377b6a92fefa369d2e" :answer/id #uuid "f6f7f173-b825-560b-a963-26cb30c2f7a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76605/selection/ea245a5fe5eff013e98e427f4cf840f7e1932397f951a41607d799d5d0a3bd26" :answer/id #uuid "fedd32ad-156e-5a3e-b2ce-d21e257ef558" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{10}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76605/selection/99c457d7d0b397201fbcdfb55bdcda505e0dd32364f14346c1013b062e1261d0" :answer/id #uuid "e45d5e38-3d88-5321-8104-53db1dfa5e20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4\\sqrt{10}}{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76605/selection/06b6df747d9be9bc8bffb00aa735b34d600558626ae3d3c6f4784da04afd96cb" :answer/id #uuid "eba81da5-0475-5477-9a6e-ab471b1ccc51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76605/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5" :answer/id #uuid "3178c751-935f-5d5c-a566-6d37c82cfe46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76605/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0d4df7d0-cf8f-5ba4-9255-96f4104da953" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76605/selection/99c457d7d0b397201fbcdfb55bdcda505e0dd32364f14346c1013b062e1261d0" :answer-field/choices ["q-76605/selection/6e19974eead0c31037cccb7d9eb05399ff73cc4f9cbc11377b6a92fefa369d2e" "q-76605/selection/ea245a5fe5eff013e98e427f4cf840f7e1932397f951a41607d799d5d0a3bd26" "q-76605/selection/99c457d7d0b397201fbcdfb55bdcda505e0dd32364f14346c1013b062e1261d0" "q-76605/selection/06b6df747d9be9bc8bffb00aa735b34d600558626ae3d3c6f4784da04afd96cb" "q-76605/selection/82f0679237d603c9b88d77fbc6f240065a24a3716631fab4d9f58426a7f011e5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76605" :question/id #uuid "a31189d8-e626-5e2f-a83b-b7786067d3b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-76605" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{C}{sec}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi (y-x)}{8})\\,\\text{d}s$ along the line segment from $(1,1)$ to $(2,4).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{t}_{a}}^{{t}_{b}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is the line segment from $(1,1)$ to $(2,4).$ \n\nThe position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=i+j$ and $b=2\\,i+4\\,j.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =(i+j)+t[2\\,i+4\\,j-(i+j)] \\\\  & =(i+j)+t(i+3\\,j) \\\\  & =(1+t)\\,i+(1+3t)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x=1+t$ and $y=1+3t$ along the segment.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+3t)j \\\\  & =1\\,i+3\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={sec}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi (y-x)}{8})$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & ={sec}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi ((1+3t)-(1+t))}{8}) \\\\  & ={sec}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}{sec}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi (y-x)}{8})\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{sec}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{4})\\cdot \\sqrt{10}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{sec}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{4})\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=\\frac{\\pi t}{4},$ $\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{10}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{sec}^{2}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{4})\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{10}}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /4}{sec}^{2}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{10}}{\\pi }\\operatorname{tan}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{10}}{\\pi }(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{10}}{\\pi }(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{10}}{\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-76605/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11fb303b-053a-56d1-9b96-acd75c748b51"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76605"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123363/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "65d190fa-d621-5731-826c-7d1e45de7a98" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123363/selection/0f4c4dd728824ee19d0a7bf37e750d49d803dbb84e7cbc9edb64740edc2f53d0" :answer/id #uuid "bc7d9ce3-90c2-5895-b7ac-bb6284a72e01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123363/selection/d5f6764a5cc10e135306591ec4dacb40918fc1a36128d20a9f7bb4063814da66" :answer/id #uuid "541c12f1-393e-559e-b066-fc62b3bafc8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{17}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123363/selection/471d022dc8477dee5b5835181abb5643fcc83818c373aaad08fa968767db722e" :answer/id #uuid "9e399984-fe60-57ac-ba03-79ba51bb85ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123363/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "5cff7979-dae4-5c6f-a554-8d5c0d5c11c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123363/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "61677e81-bc3c-56c5-9aba-8b49e44d0546" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123363/selection/0f4c4dd728824ee19d0a7bf37e750d49d803dbb84e7cbc9edb64740edc2f53d0" :answer-field/choices ["q-123363/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-123363/selection/0f4c4dd728824ee19d0a7bf37e750d49d803dbb84e7cbc9edb64740edc2f53d0" "q-123363/selection/d5f6764a5cc10e135306591ec4dacb40918fc1a36128d20a9f7bb4063814da66" "q-123363/selection/471d022dc8477dee5b5835181abb5643fcc83818c373aaad08fa968767db722e" "q-123363/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123363" :question/id #uuid "ab9316d3-2349-5452-8713-16849a27beab" :question/math-academy-id "q-123363" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral of the function $f(x,y)=x+\\sqrt{2y}$ along the line segment from $(2,0)$ to $(2,2).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{t}_{a}}^{{t}_{b}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is the line segment from $(2,0)$ to $(2,2).$ \n\nThe position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=2\\,i$ and $b=2\\,i+2\\,j.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =2\\,i+t[(2\\,i+2\\,j)-2\\,i] \\\\  & =2\\,i+2t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x=2$ and $y=2t$ along the segment.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)j \\\\  & =2j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=x+\\sqrt{2y}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =2+\\sqrt{2(2t)} \\\\  & =2+2\\sqrt{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2+2\\sqrt{t})\\cdot 2\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{1}(1+\\sqrt{t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =4{[t+\\frac{2{t}^{3/2}}{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4(1+\\frac{2}{3})-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-123363/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11fb303b-053a-56d1-9b96-acd75c748b51"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123363"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76650/selection/66443858ca2f1f35edda1428efcd3d35af39969dd5c4d8c634c9ab7e5ab1670a" :answer/id #uuid "1b552fac-410e-5af3-bea2-eb26d8e10e40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}({e}^{6}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76650/selection/1832b676f95dd3ecfa5ef6347f61bf3d0c0d456f96eaed7c2a25c608453f72ca" :answer/id #uuid "ad4bf771-f5f2-5fb4-83fe-42bfe4852a08" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}({e}^{6}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76650/selection/65c78b20ce7482b900d393ae147273288b990fac8f06edac1e5068ee063bfe4a" :answer/id #uuid "08ea5b05-df62-5298-a748-9528b4a30408" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2({e}^{6}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76650/selection/756569f23a647cbc6229945b7a42e8da0c40b890c7e69d88d4bb94e15e74be0c" :answer/id #uuid "bbd49761-2cba-5f36-9fb6-6a1498f98228" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2e\\sqrt{2}({e}^{5}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76650/selection/d0985966c5eb2c03a9a9ebdec81c326b3d1c96c024f701784837c828ec6fbb76" :answer/id #uuid "04e09432-571e-5cbd-9195-3b7f2af94d31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({e}^{6}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76650/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ef71ad3-cc87-5b91-8a6c-7e531aa8bd65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76650/selection/66443858ca2f1f35edda1428efcd3d35af39969dd5c4d8c634c9ab7e5ab1670a" :answer-field/choices ["q-76650/selection/66443858ca2f1f35edda1428efcd3d35af39969dd5c4d8c634c9ab7e5ab1670a" "q-76650/selection/1832b676f95dd3ecfa5ef6347f61bf3d0c0d456f96eaed7c2a25c608453f72ca" "q-76650/selection/65c78b20ce7482b900d393ae147273288b990fac8f06edac1e5068ee063bfe4a" "q-76650/selection/756569f23a647cbc6229945b7a42e8da0c40b890c7e69d88d4bb94e15e74be0c" "q-76650/selection/d0985966c5eb2c03a9a9ebdec81c326b3d1c96c024f701784837c828ec6fbb76"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76650" :question/id #uuid "85926769-0b89-53be-8c3d-c48574068918" :question/math-academy-id "q-76650" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{C}(4x+2)\\,{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}s$ along the line segment from $(0,1)$ to $(2,3).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{t}_{a}}^{{t}_{b}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is the line segment from $(0,1)$ to $(2,3).$ \n\nThe position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=j$ and $b=2\\,i+3\\,j.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =j+t[2\\,i+3\\,j-j] \\\\  & =j+t(2\\,i+2\\,j) \\\\  & =2t\\,i+(1+2t)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x=2t$ and $y=1+2t$ along the segment.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+2t)j \\\\  & =2\\,i+2\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=(4x+2)\\,{e}^{xy}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(4(2t)+2){e}^{2t(1+2t)} \\\\  & =(8t+2)\\,{e}^{2t+4{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(8t+2)\\,{e}^{2t+4{t}^{2}}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(8t+2)\\,{e}^{2t+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=2t+4{t}^{2},$ $\\text{d}u=(2+8t)\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(8t+2)\\,{e}^{2t+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t & =2\\sqrt{2}{\\int }_{0}^{6}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\,{e}^{u}\\,{|}_{0}^{6} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}({e}^{6}-{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}({e}^{6}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-76650/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11fb303b-053a-56d1-9b96-acd75c748b51"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76650"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123366/selection/99be353997b3ae8daee1a55922806b31687c556e62c9cfd57add7ce0ca959a98" :answer/id #uuid "c9805760-367f-5345-99c6-e49894c7d88e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4e-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123366/selection/e778296658ef4a275b9622bb91a50e55ce2e3e3d8e5e920daf13339dd12b5611" :answer/id #uuid "4560359d-beae-5e58-804e-f3646504db07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}({e}^{2}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123366/selection/7c676f7615623e470dce2f468ed37f8954ab734da539ca365b29c20596ba5e04" :answer/id #uuid "46922c83-3bd3-5672-bcb1-e6c8149407d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4({e}^{2}-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123366/selection/51ea1925b5d90dd40c85e316bc1e6833b888f9f56700d9941c17a681b1da3194" :answer/id #uuid "fedd089a-c272-58f1-a5a7-49599f7fd36b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}(e-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123366/selection/cf60bdf0310731009b56663194c647265b54eebc087185b30be4afcacd9318be" :answer/id #uuid "8fd9c9e5-8ec6-5669-b42e-7028f7c3a134" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4(e-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123366/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eef7246e-e49b-5e18-a62b-9f92dda35c18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123366/selection/51ea1925b5d90dd40c85e316bc1e6833b888f9f56700d9941c17a681b1da3194" :answer-field/choices ["q-123366/selection/99be353997b3ae8daee1a55922806b31687c556e62c9cfd57add7ce0ca959a98" "q-123366/selection/e778296658ef4a275b9622bb91a50e55ce2e3e3d8e5e920daf13339dd12b5611" "q-123366/selection/7c676f7615623e470dce2f468ed37f8954ab734da539ca365b29c20596ba5e04" "q-123366/selection/51ea1925b5d90dd40c85e316bc1e6833b888f9f56700d9941c17a681b1da3194" "q-123366/selection/cf60bdf0310731009b56663194c647265b54eebc087185b30be4afcacd9318be"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123366" :question/id #uuid "2981ab75-efc9-5bfb-9a41-86f5110c9734" :question/math-academy-id "q-123366" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral of the function $f(x,y)={e}^{3x+y}$ along the line segment from $(0,0)$ to $(-1,4).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{t}_{a}}^{{t}_{b}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is the line segment from $(0,0)$ to $(-1,4).$ \n\nThe position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=0$ and $b=-i+4\\,j.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =0+t\\,(b-0) \\\\  & =t\\,(b) \\\\  & =t(-i+4\\,j) \\\\  & =-t\\,i+4t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x=-t$ and $y=4t$ along the segment.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t)j \\\\  & =-i+4\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)={e}^{3x+y}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & ={e}^{3(-t)+4t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{t}\\cdot \\sqrt{17}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17}[{e}^{t}]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17}(e-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-123366/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11fb303b-053a-56d1-9b96-acd75c748b51"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123366"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76564/selection/733e946ee12fd282b8e2c94b5bf21ec2fc9d45de53807f39ee69226f39b6d624" :answer/id #uuid "b1a3d3d1-20c8-55a0-8cbc-3804d0b2b5e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{34}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76564/selection/f169f92c1946b4a86dcd40a5cae1a30ea50a84a49ecc59038782fea0bf2058cc" :answer/id #uuid "0d32f231-967e-585e-8439-a3f1ce405226" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76564/selection/df988b403d3badcdb3336fe30e0018c50b98820520ae8679b58e51a9bb9f6fd5" :answer/id #uuid "bbed7783-c336-5a5b-8670-f965d3c4e39c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25\\sqrt{34}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76564/selection/cd30ed0490ce1b12eaef8de2ac647121a762b197d4ac28233e89b65639429bdc" :answer/id #uuid "61096aa9-27ca-57df-b8d0-cab2c4d4344d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25\\sqrt{34}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76564/selection/72d185db80ed497ec9f30fc3aee54a6761fdd2306b416e2cdafd78556117e9a4" :answer/id #uuid "a1f0ada8-bef1-5224-8982-943064d76846" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{34}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76564/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7f2ff920-1d53-52b1-9c49-48b7a5e8f22a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76564/selection/cd30ed0490ce1b12eaef8de2ac647121a762b197d4ac28233e89b65639429bdc" :answer-field/choices ["q-76564/selection/733e946ee12fd282b8e2c94b5bf21ec2fc9d45de53807f39ee69226f39b6d624" "q-76564/selection/f169f92c1946b4a86dcd40a5cae1a30ea50a84a49ecc59038782fea0bf2058cc" "q-76564/selection/df988b403d3badcdb3336fe30e0018c50b98820520ae8679b58e51a9bb9f6fd5" "q-76564/selection/cd30ed0490ce1b12eaef8de2ac647121a762b197d4ac28233e89b65639429bdc" "q-76564/selection/72d185db80ed497ec9f30fc3aee54a6761fdd2306b416e2cdafd78556117e9a4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76564" :question/id #uuid "dc4eb82b-0fb4-5ee9-a8d9-88ec2a1d3fe4" :question/math-academy-id "q-76564" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral of the function $f(x,y)=xy$ along the line segment from $(1,2)$ to $(4,7).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{t}_{a}}^{{t}_{b}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is the line segment from $(1,2)$ to $(4,7).$\n\nThe position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=i+2\\,j$ and $b=4\\,i+7j.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =(i+2\\,j)+t[4\\,i+7j-(i+2\\,j)] \\\\  & =(i+2\\,j)+t(3i+5j) \\\\  & =(1+3t)\\,i+(2+5t)\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x=1+3t$ and $y=2+5t$ along the segment.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+3t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2+5t)j \\\\  & =3i+5j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y)=xy$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(1+3t)(2+5t) \\\\  & =15{t}^{2}+11t+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(15{t}^{2}+11t+2)\\cdot \\sqrt{34}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(15{t}^{2}+11t+2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34}{[5{t}^{3}+\\frac{11}{2}{t}^{2}+2t]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34}(5+\\frac{11}{2}+2)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{25\\sqrt{34}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-76564/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "11fb303b-053a-56d1-9b96-acd75c748b51"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76564"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76569/selection/9398d32e799aa57b7f840d3929a3c5ab47f479fdcf5e16d9c3df4f9709d0f64c" :answer/id #uuid "c4fb6e27-079a-5a2a-84a4-fa0dd95c16fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76569/selection/4b327bb8be2f61f30ea5a92f1cf5fe303317fa2d050b514d221a066373c038be" :answer/id #uuid "ec220981-193e-5b88-bd4a-e19c5e9d0a30" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13\\sqrt{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76569/selection/718ff1f1e9146b5d5d2cf798138ec0393245e544620d23b1f48534b92efd546a" :answer/id #uuid "4ee97f54-7edd-5f60-a512-0be454d0613b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76569/selection/6d859a59ce4da7d9346e4130432a6746c9d659404b98f425494a826f9993f794" :answer/id #uuid "14cf8615-48cd-5cbf-b07e-40c20cb5003c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13\\sqrt{11}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76569/selection/3ddde6d65b57504d7927970030ff6f47cc633268963c87eff4ee46a732086804" :answer/id #uuid "1e5bb937-5155-5dd3-b17a-31546736d8a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76569/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d078ca79-3f43-5bf4-8022-abe848a8f043" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76569/selection/6d859a59ce4da7d9346e4130432a6746c9d659404b98f425494a826f9993f794" :answer-field/choices ["q-76569/selection/9398d32e799aa57b7f840d3929a3c5ab47f479fdcf5e16d9c3df4f9709d0f64c" "q-76569/selection/4b327bb8be2f61f30ea5a92f1cf5fe303317fa2d050b514d221a066373c038be" "q-76569/selection/718ff1f1e9146b5d5d2cf798138ec0393245e544620d23b1f48534b92efd546a" "q-76569/selection/6d859a59ce4da7d9346e4130432a6746c9d659404b98f425494a826f9993f794" "q-76569/selection/3ddde6d65b57504d7927970030ff6f47cc633268963c87eff4ee46a732086804"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76569" :question/id #uuid "99240e72-b8a8-53f0-b2dc-5d4737a02b38" :question/math-academy-id "q-76569" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{C}x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}s$ along the line segment from $(1,2,0)$ to $(2,1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{t}_{a}}^{{t}_{b}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is the line segment from$(1,2,0)$ to $(2,1,3).$\n\nThe position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=i+2\\,j$ and $b=2\\,i+j+3\\,k.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =(i+2\\,j)+t[(2\\,i+j+3\\,k)-(i+2\\,j)] \\\\  & =(i+2\\,j)+t(i-j+3\\,k) \\\\  & =(1+t)\\,i+(2-t)\\,j+3t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x=1+t,$ $y=2-t,$ and $z=3t$ along the segment.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2-t)j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t)k \\\\  & =i-j+3\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{11}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y,z)=x{y}^{2}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(1+t)(2-t)^{2} \\\\  & ={t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+4)\\cdot \\sqrt{11}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{11}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+4)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{11}{[\\frac{{t}^{4}}{4}-{t}^{3}+4t]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{11}(\\frac{1}{4}-1+4)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\sqrt{11}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-76569/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14ab317b-fd33-5d6e-9d54-87e749b78283"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76569"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123387/selection/17d4229a34d09d03c946a0512b5f51c409942e21567e5de35be2872134a58547" :answer/id #uuid "3209c569-1111-5f5f-8cac-dc96a7707b04" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{21}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123387/selection/54df50d2e1fb1ccc3e38b66d2bfeb3eb1324f055c3df1a06e09e1b9ba63f52ad" :answer/id #uuid "b07adc66-f9b3-5898-b079-d0fdcad0d163" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}t\\sqrt{t-1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123387/selection/cdde6b598c9e8cf73284555ff3a349f25cc8520663464386af9717d471e2cc45" :answer/id #uuid "5fa4eda7-bc03-5ce7-8340-13ba4826603c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{21}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123387/selection/2a4f99f7b3cd401a979056b5b6192d2a3ab4b16d1da6520d470e7c5099bff11b" :answer/id #uuid "de421106-059a-582e-8143-54ab1cc886b9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{21}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123387/selection/a25e66160c32b08fa10568202a6acc0b93fa462787e00781eb87e697284341df" :answer/id #uuid "0ea029af-309f-5f4e-807a-5d1890c7fc2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{5t-3}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123387/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ca2c18be-37dd-5683-aed7-9be97559fde8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123387/selection/cdde6b598c9e8cf73284555ff3a349f25cc8520663464386af9717d471e2cc45" :answer-field/choices ["q-123387/selection/17d4229a34d09d03c946a0512b5f51c409942e21567e5de35be2872134a58547" "q-123387/selection/54df50d2e1fb1ccc3e38b66d2bfeb3eb1324f055c3df1a06e09e1b9ba63f52ad" "q-123387/selection/cdde6b598c9e8cf73284555ff3a349f25cc8520663464386af9717d471e2cc45" "q-123387/selection/2a4f99f7b3cd401a979056b5b6192d2a3ab4b16d1da6520d470e7c5099bff11b" "q-123387/selection/a25e66160c32b08fa10568202a6acc0b93fa462787e00781eb87e697284341df"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123387" :question/id #uuid "963025de-8b37-535e-a08b-0b16983c48ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-123387" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the line integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{2x+y-z},$ traversed along the line segment from $(3,-2,3)$ to $(5,-1,7)?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{t}_{a}}^{{t}_{b}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is the line segment from $(3,-2,3)$ to $(5,-1,7).$\n\nThe position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=3i-2\\,j+3k$ and $b=5\\,i-j+7\\,k.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =(3i-2\\,j+3k)+t[(5\\,i-j+7\\,k)-(3i-2\\,j+3k)] \\\\  & =(3i-2\\,j+3k)+t(2i+\\,j+4k) \\\\  & =(2t+3)\\,i+(t-2)\\,j+(4t+3)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x=2t+3,y=t-2,$ and $z=4t+3$ along the segment.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t+3)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-2)j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t+3)k \\\\  & =2i+j+4\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{21}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y,z)=\\sqrt{2x+y-z}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\sqrt{2(2t+3)+(t-2)-(4t+3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{t+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{t+1}\\cdot \\sqrt{21}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{21}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-123387/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14ab317b-fd33-5d6e-9d54-87e749b78283"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123387"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76577/selection/a8b2dd902249eebc328e881b5ce14c101d2f04138c66948b353b0c49986bd4f7" :answer/id #uuid "7f4efd7b-bc80-500f-9ebf-544ece667d44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76577/selection/513f1544cffee11f5250a07a8cfbc5237cc1f519686a340fcc741256b0b49f3d" :answer/id #uuid "3adedde5-2966-5494-b62f-35270cabd8a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76577/selection/2281ad44b7a1ae0b287bdbb4c16b036589dede1f6bafd135faf87db2eecc70c8" :answer/id #uuid "4ed95bc1-1125-5c37-98b5-ccec57391dbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{5\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76577/selection/1670efabd98488feb647873cbae5aa6c666005ce195d7c9abdcf1cfe0acc3ec1" :answer/id #uuid "5d8b0c96-58d6-5c23-9662-54cd05410af4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{3\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76577/selection/6274bf0ffc8f1637b60076c3a8812c9070903a62ed7318909a067853c529f9d5" :answer/id #uuid "86fd7f7f-a388-5ba0-8a1d-7e7672527f9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3\\pi }" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76577/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6949ba0-743e-5a2a-8337-754903704af7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76577/selection/1670efabd98488feb647873cbae5aa6c666005ce195d7c9abdcf1cfe0acc3ec1" :answer-field/choices ["q-76577/selection/a8b2dd902249eebc328e881b5ce14c101d2f04138c66948b353b0c49986bd4f7" "q-76577/selection/513f1544cffee11f5250a07a8cfbc5237cc1f519686a340fcc741256b0b49f3d" "q-76577/selection/2281ad44b7a1ae0b287bdbb4c16b036589dede1f6bafd135faf87db2eecc70c8" "q-76577/selection/1670efabd98488feb647873cbae5aa6c666005ce195d7c9abdcf1cfe0acc3ec1" "q-76577/selection/6274bf0ffc8f1637b60076c3a8812c9070903a62ed7318909a067853c529f9d5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76577" :question/id #uuid "409db294-5a4c-56d9-9c78-1266cf72e579" :question/math-academy-id "q-76577" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{C}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}(x+z))\\,\\text{d}s$ along the line segment from $(-1,2,1)$ to $(1,2,5).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{t}_{a}}^{{t}_{b}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is the line segment from $(-1,2,1)$ to $(1,2,5).$ \n\nThe position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=-i+2\\,j+k$ and $b=i+2\\,j+5\\,k.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =(-i+2\\,j+k)+t[(i+2\\,j+5\\,k)-(-i+2\\,j+k)] \\\\  & =(-i+2\\,j+k)+t(2\\,i+4\\,k) \\\\  & =(-1+2t)\\,i+2\\,j+(1+4t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x=-1+2t,$ $y=2,$ and $z=1+4t$ along the segment.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-1+2t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1+4t)k \\\\  & =2\\,i+0+4\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y,z)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}(x+z))$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}((-1+2t)+(1+4t))) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi t}{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}(x+z))\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi t}{2})\\cdot 2\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi t}{2})\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=\\frac{3\\pi t}{2}$, $\\text{d}u=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi t}{2})\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{3\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{3\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{3\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{3\\pi }(-1-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{3\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-76577/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14ab317b-fd33-5d6e-9d54-87e749b78283"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76577"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123434/selection/7493c55899987356b0e413488903d5e4e608fe11b7a30e6a09d588368d748962" :answer/id #uuid "83f77d7e-0799-5dc5-bfff-89707dd58b97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{3}+1}{{e}^{5}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123434/selection/e1d2fdaf7934e58e6d0442c97dd21588359932fd125cf3114116bad4bb10d4a9" :answer/id #uuid "5018526b-1027-52c3-8d5b-508e32bd3a5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}({e}^{2}-1)}{{e}^{3}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123434/selection/f2169887e78eed866ddfdcdc911ce0c7d792e266eb752598a5496c50ce3f4b01" :answer/id #uuid "056208db-66d2-5c48-8a9a-664e7d64b51a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}({e}^{3}-1)}{{e}^{8}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123434/selection/5bee346e04b9613d9e20eb791fa586872c368594afab0a0dd576793665ed3520" :answer/id #uuid "3b03d2b2-d87e-571e-ad8e-5b11af008bcb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}({e}^{3}+2)}{{e}^{8}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123434/selection/e5a2f2ede364b3e646d8bcb2cc6ca35b0a1e2541a4deb10a9b87024a02bacfc9" :answer/id #uuid "a345c2ab-fa32-560d-9ace-e78b27e74536" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{3}-1}{{e}^{8}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123434/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "39581479-a175-530a-a7e5-ccb7e347d3cf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123434/selection/f2169887e78eed866ddfdcdc911ce0c7d792e266eb752598a5496c50ce3f4b01" :answer-field/choices ["q-123434/selection/7493c55899987356b0e413488903d5e4e608fe11b7a30e6a09d588368d748962" "q-123434/selection/e1d2fdaf7934e58e6d0442c97dd21588359932fd125cf3114116bad4bb10d4a9" "q-123434/selection/f2169887e78eed866ddfdcdc911ce0c7d792e266eb752598a5496c50ce3f4b01" "q-123434/selection/5bee346e04b9613d9e20eb791fa586872c368594afab0a0dd576793665ed3520" "q-123434/selection/e5a2f2ede364b3e646d8bcb2cc6ca35b0a1e2541a4deb10a9b87024a02bacfc9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123434" :question/id #uuid "1a241751-b914-599a-9968-6041dee04727" :question/math-academy-id "q-123434" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral ${\\int }_{C}x{e}^{yz}\\,\\text{d}s$ along the line segment from $(2,-2,4)$ to $(4,-1,5).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{t}_{a}}^{{t}_{b}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is the line segment from $(2,-2,4)$ to $(4,-1,5).$ \n\nThe position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=2\\,i-2\\,j+4\\,k$ and $b=4\\,i-\\,j+5\\,k.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =(2\\,i-2\\,j+4\\,k)+t[(4\\,i-\\,j+5\\,k)-(2\\,i-2\\,j+4\\,k)] \\\\  & =(2\\,i-2\\,j+4\\,k)+t(2\\,i+j+k) \\\\  & =(2t+2)\\,i+(t-2)\\,j+(t+4)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x=2t+2,$ $y=t-2,$ and $z=t+4$ along the segment.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t+2)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-2)j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+4)k \\\\  & =2\\,i+j+k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y,z)=x{e}^{yz}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(2t+2){e}^{(t-2)(t+4)} \\\\  & =(2t+2){e}^{{t}^{2}+2t-8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}x{e}^{yz}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2t+2){e}^{{t}^{2}+2t-8}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2t+2){e}^{{t}^{2}+2t-8}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u={t}^{2}+2t-8$, $\\text{d}u=(2t+2)\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(2t+2){e}^{{t}^{2}+2t-8}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\sqrt{6}\\,{\\int }_{-8}^{-5}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\,{e}^{u}\\,{|}_{-8}^{-5} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}({e}^{-5}-{e}^{-8}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}(\\frac{1}{{e}^{5}}-\\frac{1}{{e}^{8}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{6}({e}^{3}-1)}{{e}^{8}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-123434/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14ab317b-fd33-5d6e-9d54-87e749b78283"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123434"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-123431/selection/e2c450f6b0bb66ae47b9d67933f90c252fe85c5ec6289226f28e0c43e30efacf" :answer/id #uuid "6e8d7d20-6ef5-56df-bcdf-aff394d38f52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{2t-1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123431/selection/40d7379ad1d3cd652ae4fe894c751f54c0f08ddcbe686313a9ee3ac3715b897d" :answer/id #uuid "2e4c1837-67c3-5963-883b-0045a38ad11a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{2t+1}{t-1}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123431/selection/37238acf201dbe55353ce7e3c0a79628634671f63d8838ed585039b177715996" :answer/id #uuid "2669a665-aa78-5548-9d98-8d1ed6b32680" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{t}{t-2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123431/selection/89a76acd5b9ac9d04752c02c7d2e3ef75ad070da9a75931a21cf1eba002ce34c" :answer/id #uuid "5d623bf7-63fa-50b7-afb8-451c11b3f9de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{t-2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123431/selection/0aab89f5a7a90d1ea308453872a9ed54a211335d0b0966c91a7c8d90037e35de" :answer/id #uuid "cff81bdf-2450-5905-8726-398e96ac5c01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+2}\\,\\text{d}t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-123431/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a7ab9bad-069e-5b7e-af10-a7fbd6f4a7fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-123431/selection/89a76acd5b9ac9d04752c02c7d2e3ef75ad070da9a75931a21cf1eba002ce34c" :answer-field/choices ["q-123431/selection/e2c450f6b0bb66ae47b9d67933f90c252fe85c5ec6289226f28e0c43e30efacf" "q-123431/selection/40d7379ad1d3cd652ae4fe894c751f54c0f08ddcbe686313a9ee3ac3715b897d" "q-123431/selection/37238acf201dbe55353ce7e3c0a79628634671f63d8838ed585039b177715996" "q-123431/selection/89a76acd5b9ac9d04752c02c7d2e3ef75ad070da9a75931a21cf1eba002ce34c" "q-123431/selection/0aab89f5a7a90d1ea308453872a9ed54a211335d0b0966c91a7c8d90037e35de"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-123431" :question/id #uuid "3f3b2749-1e0f-5594-900d-79f43f56ef7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-123431" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to the line integral of the function $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{y+z}{x},$ traversed along the line segment from $(-4,1,5)$ to $(-2,3,3)?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{t}_{a}}^{{t}_{b}}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is the line segment from $(-4,1,5)$ to $(-2,3,3).$\n\nThe position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $a=-4i+j+5\\,k$ and $b=-2\\,i+3\\,j+3\\,k.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =(-4i+j+5\\,k)+t[(-2\\,i+3\\,j+3\\,k)-(-4i+j+5\\,k)] \\\\  & =(-4i+j+5\\,k)+t(2i+2\\,j-2\\,k) \\\\  & =(2t-4)\\,i+(2t+1)\\,j+(5-2t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0\\le t\\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x=2t-4,y=2t+1,$ and $z=5-2t$ along the segment.\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t-4)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t+1)j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5-2t)k \\\\  & =2\\,i+2\\,j-2\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{y+z}{x}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =\\frac{(2t+1)+(5-2t)}{2t-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{2t-4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{t-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{3}{t-2}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{t-2}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-123431/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "14ab317b-fd33-5d6e-9d54-87e749b78283"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-123431"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9486"] :question/problem "Find a definite integral that is equivalent to the line integral of the function $f(x,y) = x+\\sin{y},$ traversed along the line segment from $(1,0)$ to $(1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C f(x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}s  =  \\int\\limits_{t_a}^{t_b}  f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\, \\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\| \\, \\textrm{d}t,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is the line segment from $(1,0)$ to $(1,1).$ \n\nThe position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $\\mathbf{a}=\\mathbf{i}$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =i+t[(i+j)-i] \\\\  & =i+t\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0 \\le t \\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x=1$ and $y=t$ along the segment.\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and $\\| \\mathbf{r}'(t) \\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)j \\\\  & =0\\,i+j \\\\  & =j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y) = x+\\sin{y}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot 1\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-6304"] :question/problem "Evaluate the integral of the function $f(x,y) = e^{x+y}$ along the line segment from $(0,3)$ to $(2,3).$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C f(x, y) \\, \\textrm{d}s  = \\int\\limits_{t_a}^{t_b}  f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\, \\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\| \\, \\textrm{d}t,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is the line segment from $(0,3)$ to $(2,3).$ \n\nThe position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $\\mathbf{a}=3\\,\\mathbf{j}$ and $\\mathbf{b}=2\\,\\mathbf{i}+3\\,\\mathbf{j}.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =3\\,j+t[(2\\,i+3\\,j)-3\\,j] \\\\  & =3\\,j+t(2\\,i) \\\\  & =2t\\,i+3\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0 \\le t \\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x=2t$ and $y=3$ along the segment.\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and $\\| \\mathbf{r}'(t) \\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3)j \\\\  & =2\\,i \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y) = e^{x+y},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & ={e}^{2t+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}{e}^{x+y}\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{2t+3}\\cdot 2\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{2t+3}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=2t+3,$ $\\textrm d u=2\\,\\textrm d t$ as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{2t+3}\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\,{|}_{3}^{5} \\\\  & ={e}^{5}-{e}^{3} \\\\  & ={e}^{3}({e}^{2}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-9487"] :question/problem "Find the line integral of the function $f(x,y,z) = x^2+y-z,$ traversed along the line segment from $(0,1,-3)$ to $(-1,2,-2)?$" :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C f(x,y,z) \\, \\textrm{d}s  =  \\int\\limits_{t_a}^{t_b}  f(\\mathbf r(t)) \\, \\| \\mathbf r'(t) \\| \\, \\textrm{d}t,\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere $C$ is the line segment from $(0,1,-3)$ to $(-1,2,-2).$\n\nThe position vectors of the endpoints of our line segment are $\\mathbf{a}=\\mathbf{j}-3\\mathbf{k}$ and $\\mathbf{b}=-\\,\\mathbf{i}+2\\,\\mathbf{j}-2\\,\\mathbf{k}.$ So, the parametrization of the line segment is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =a+t\\,(b-a) \\\\  & =(j-3k)+t[(-\\,i+2\\,j-2\\,k)-(j-3k)] \\\\  & =(j-3k)+t(-i+\\,j+k) \\\\  & =-t\\,i+(t+1)\\,j+(t-3)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $0 \\le t \\le 1.$ Thus, we have that $x=-t, y=t+1,$ and $z=t-3$ along the segment.\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and $\\| \\mathbf{r}'(t) \\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t)i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1)j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t-3)k \\\\  & =-i+j+k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}+{(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y) = x^2+y-z$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(t)) & =(-t)^{2}+(t+1)-(t-3) \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(r(t))\\,‖{r}^{′}(t)‖\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({t}^{2}+4)\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({t}^{2}+4)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
